ernia: no respiratory distress described"], "alarm_features": ["Down syndrome physical features (increased risk for Hirschsprung's disease)", "Neonatal intestinal obstruction (high-risk condition requiring urgent evaluation)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Structural Gastrointestinal Obstruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.44148563419761744, "posterior": 0.1884889854173131, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal prenatal imaging provides minimal evidence against other congenital anomalies in this clinical context."], "evidence_against": ["Spontaneous stool evacuation suggests partial patency, weakly favoring functional over complete structural obstruction."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Functional Gastrointestinal Obstruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3153468815697268, "posterior": 0.23852001241079746, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal prenatal imaging provides minimal evidence against other congenital anomalies in this clinical context."], "evidence_against": ["Meconium absence reduces likelihood of Hirschsprung disease but is not definitive due to limited diagnostic power."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Congenital Malrotation Syndromes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "